{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1480475-synthesis-and-the-living","id":1480475,"title":"Synthesis and the Living","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-08T13:37:39-07:00","id":1480475,"title":"Synthesis and the Living","content":"So...what I am wondering is what happens when a Strix uses synthesis on a living body but without killing it or killing itself. Like it places some of the shadow potency within the body of a living body and then is ejected...but I wonder how that affects someone beyond the damage they take per success?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-08T14:05:09-07:00","id":1480477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1480475-synthesis-and-the-living#post1480475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So...what I am wondering is what happens when a Strix uses synthesis on a living body but without killing it or killing itself. Like it places some of the shadow potency within the body of a living body and then is ejected...but I wonder how that affects someone beyond the damage they take per success?</div> </div> </div> </div>The boring answer is: It doesn't. The difference between a Synthesized corpse host and a Synthesized living host is a matter of timing and leftover humanity; if the process doesn't kill the host, the only change is that they're closer to death.<br /> <br /> Alternately, because this reading is equally thematic: Nothing in the text says that the process of Synthesis has to be what kills the host and causes it to rise as Kindred the next night. A living person infused with Shadow Potency will rise as a vampire after they are killed, regardless of when that happens, and they will be better able to blend in with the herd, as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-08T18:40:29-07:00","id":1480501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1480475-synthesis-and-the-living?p=1480477#post1480477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The boring answer is: It doesn't. The difference between a Synthesized corpse host and a Synthesized living host is a matter of timing and leftover humanity; if the process doesn't kill the host, the only change is that they're closer to death.<br /> <br /> Alternately, because this reading is equally thematic: Nothing in the text says that the process of Synthesis has to be what kills the host and causes it to rise as Kindred the next night. A living person infused with Shadow Potency will rise as a vampire after they are killed, regardless of when that happens, and they will be better able to blend in with the herd, as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well the thing that makes it seem less interesting to me is that when done to a supernatural creature aberrant powers and creatures are created as a result. So one would think that even if it doesn't kill the living host that it would have some kind of effect while they are alive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-08T21:07:33-07:00","id":1480510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1480475-synthesis-and-the-living?p=1480501#post1480501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the thing that makes it seem less interesting to me is that when done to a supernatural creature aberrant powers and creatures are created as a result. So one would think that even if it doesn't kill the living host that it would have some kind of effect while they are alive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Synthesizing a living host takes twenty successes on an extended roll that can only be rolled for once per night, living hosts do not provide access to their supernatural powers normally, the initial possession inflicts lethal damage and while possessed the host can be reflexively damaged for Vitae, and the most &quot;successful&quot; Synthesis is one where the Strix ceases to exist as a separate being and instead a new less-human vampire is created. If the Strix wants the process to kill the host, it can do so basically at will.<br /> <br /> Cases where Synthesis isn't used to get the Strix a permanent body are instead the stuff of the Julii's founding myth, where the body is infused with the Beast and able to become a proper vampire, which seems unlikely to be an offer the Owls will make to things that aren't vampires \u2014 recall that their standard interpretation of bargains for power is to possess the querent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-09T00:10:38-07:00","id":1480518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1480475-synthesis-and-the-living?p=1480510#post1480510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Synthesizing a living host takes twenty successes on an extended roll that can only be rolled for once per night, living hosts do not provide access to their supernatural powers normally, the initial possession inflicts lethal damage and while possessed the host can be reflexively damaged for Vitae, and the most &quot;successful&quot; Synthesis is one where the Strix ceases to exist as a separate being and instead a new less-human vampire is created. If the Strix wants the process to kill the host, it can do so basically at will.<br /> <br /> Cases where Synthesis isn't used to get the Strix a permanent body are instead the stuff of the Julii's founding myth, where the body is infused with the Beast and able to become a proper vampire, which seems unlikely to be an offer the Owls will make to things that aren't vampires \u2014 recall that their standard interpretation of bargains for power is to possess the querent.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> &quot;Where things get really strange is if the Strix then attempts to use Synthesis on a supernatural host. Unique monsters and aberrant powers result. &quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-09T00:14:12-07:00","id":1480519,"title":"","content":"A funny thing I realized while looking at synthesis is that when it is used on a corpse host it creates a vampire universally. Which is funny because that would then also happen if a strix used synthesis on an animal corpse it was possessing since the description didn't provide an alternative for what it would do if the host body wasn't human in that case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-09T03:21:21-07:00","id":1480521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1480475-synthesis-and-the-living?p=1480519#post1480519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A funny thing I realized while looking at synthesis is that when it is used on a corpse host it creates a vampire universally. Which is funny because that would then also happen if a strix used synthesis on an animal corpse it was possessing since the description didn't provide an alternative for what it would do if the host body wasn't human in that case.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, are Strix ever described possessing animal carcasses in the first place?<br /> Because i honestly remember no iteration of such a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-09-2022, 06:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-09T05:28:24-07:00","id":1480524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1480475-synthesis-and-the-living?p=1480521#post1480521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, are Strix ever described possessing animal carcasses in the first place?<br /> Because i honestly remember no iteration of such a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a Strix called the Black Cat in the core book that possesses animals exclusively","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-09T06:41:25-07:00","id":1480530,"title":"","content":"yeah black cat possess animals exclusively and they don't have the shadow potency to possess a living creature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-09T14:56:18-07:00","id":1480581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1480475-synthesis-and-the-living?p=1480518#post1480518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Where things get really strange is if the Strix then attempts to use Synthesis on a supernatural host. Unique monsters and aberrant powers result. &quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I read that part while checking the text. You'll notice that that doesn't contradict a single thing I said \u2014 supernatural hosts are not immune to death by exsanguination/life-draining while unconscious.<br /> <br /> Maybe this is a route to weird bootleg Tremere, Devourers, or other Night Horrors phenomena, if one doesn't want to go through the trouble of going full-homebrew, but nothing about using Synthesis on a supernatural living host requires the host to survive the process for it to create a weird outcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-28T18:56:19-07:00","id":1485244,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\">I remember reading on the rppgnet forums that if the Strix is ejected or destroyed, it still leaves behind a tiny bit of itself that is too small to make any difference. But...<br /> <br /> There's this line on p. 234 &quot;Some Kindred theorize that the minds of the Strix become confused when not in host bodies, warping memory the way some disorders affect Kindred in torpor.&quot;<br /> <br /> So maybe we can say that a Strix's memories of their time unembodied aren't as stable as the memories they create and access while embodied. If so, it might be a fun plot to have a human survive a Synthesis attempt, who then lives with a tiny, silent hitch hiker, slowly forgetting its other life and learning how its new host acts. Then, when the host dies, the corpse rises as a Revenant, animated by a Strix who thinks its the original human. As time goes on, it becomes clear that the Revenant's personality has changed since life. The Revenant has dreams of flight. It doesn't seem to have all of the original person's memories. Maybe the Reve-strix has a moment of horrible self-actualization as it realizes it doesn't want or have need to be bound by morality.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T04:11:47-07:00","id":1485274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1480475-synthesis-and-the-living?p=1480530#post1480530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yeah black cat possess animals exclusively and they don't have the shadow potency to possess a living creature.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Interesting to know. Skinchangers has a south american jaguar spirit, the <i>Kanaima</i>, who will avenge grievances against the dead by raising their corpses as bloodthirsty shapechanging undead, making a pretty interesting alternative to the Strix as patron of certain revenants or kindred.<br /> <br /> Not to mention a good monkeywrench to throw in the way of lore-versed players who might read signs of the Owls in some of clues and hints, only to then meet something else altogether and that works with somewhat different interests and mindset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-29-2022, 07:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}